---
pagination: { data: languages, size: 1, alias: lang }
permalink: "{{ '/' if lang == 'en' else '/es/' }}index.html"
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: home
descKey: home.meta_desc
pageScripts: ["/assets/vendor/lite-yt-embed.js", "/assets/js/home.js", "/assets/js/shop.js"]
pageStyles: ["/assets/css/home.css", "/assets/vendor/lite-yt-embed.css"]
---
{#- ======================================================================
    HOME PAGE — NETA 65 Grapevine / La Viña Committee (EN + ES)
    Short on purpose (the UX review of November 2026: the page was 14,240 px tall on a phone — 16 screens —
    with 14 sections and 207 links). Seven blocks, each a way in to the page that holds the whole of it:
      1. the hero (ui.pageHero): what the site is, "Find an AA meeting near you" (aa.org's own finder,
         config/site.yml links.aa_find) and What's new; from 1024px our two monthly meetings on the right (the next
         committee meeting's card with its countdown, then the next Grapevine Meeting's);
      2. under the hero (page-overlap): the same two meeting cards below 1024px, then "Where would you like to
         start?" — four big buttons, "I'm new to AA" first (the "New to AA?" first-steps card on
         /meetings/#new-to-aa: Home's one link there, high on the page), a group rep, writing, subscribing;
      3. the daily quote (Grapevine's Daily Quote and La Viña's Cita Diaria);
      4. the latest magazines: three stories of each, and this month's Book of the Month while it is on;
      5. listen & watch: the newest podcast episode (it plays here) beside "More episodes" (three, each a play
         button for the episode card's player), and under them the newest video as one compact strip;
      6. the next three events;
      7. "More on this site": one row of links to the pages that were sections here before — the Bulletin,
         the Library, Published writers, Instagram, the Portfolio, Photos — and Stay updated.
    Every section reads synced data through `D` (= db | homeData) and is left out when it has no data — Home
    never shows an empty section. Each opens with ui.sectionHead (eyebrow form, its tone colour, the "all" link
    on the right). Headings: the hero's <h1>, then one <h2> per section, in page order (the meeting cards' titles
    are an <h2> only in their below-1024px copy — the hero's copy names its card with a <p>, so the outline never
    holds the same heading twice).
    Its styles are a stylesheet of its own (/assets/css/home.css: areas/home.css), linked only here.
    The hero art (hero-canvas.js) is loaded by layouts/base.njk on every page.
    Between the daily builds (and in a copy kept for offline use) what has ended hides itself: each upcoming
    event carries data-gv-expire (homeEventEnd) and the events section is data-gv-expire-list (it goes once all
    of its cards have: src/assets/js/app.js GV.expire, checked every minute); so does the write button's "Next
    deadline" line (fsDayEnd).
    ====================================================================== -#}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{% set L = lang %}
{% set D = db | homeData %}
{#- Podcast shows, as on /listen/ (AA Grapevine's Podcast + the recordings of the two weekly open
    meetings, Grapevine's and La Viña's): name, language, short name and its language. Episode / video titles use
    the shared `mediaTitle` filter, so they read the same as on /listen/ and /watch/. -#}
{% set epShows = D.episodes | mediaShowList(site.sources.podcasts, D.episodes | mediaItems("episodes"), L) %}

{#- ---------- local macros ---------- -#}

{#- Remote images can vanish (expired CDN links, private Drive files): drop them and let the tile underneath show
    (the tiles of "More episodes"). -#}
{% macro img(src, cls="", alt="") %}<img src="{{ src }}" alt="{{ alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" class="{{ cls }}" onerror="this.remove()">{% endmacro %}

{#- Compact "next committee meeting" card with a live countdown (home.js → homeMeeting).
    v = "hero": dark glass, in the hero's right column (1024px and up);
    v = "page": light card right below the hero (below 1024px). Only one of the two is
    ever displayed, so each has its own heading id — and only the "page" copy's title is an <h2> (the hero's is a
    <p>: the same words as a second heading made the page's outline name the card twice). The meeting code is on
    /meetings/ ("Details"); the link (site.meeting.online_url) is all it takes to join. The next meeting's guest
    speaker and topic (src/_data/meeting.js: none on a date without one); `spk` = the speakers to come
    (committee.js cmSpeakers), so the card shows the right one — or none — once home.js rolls it on to the next
    date. In the hero the topic keeps to one line (two below the hero): the hero holds the Grapevine Meeting's card
    too (gvmCard, next), and the whole topic is on /meetings/. -#}
{% macro meetingCard(v, L, meeting, mt, spk) %}
{%- set dark = v == "hero" -%}
{%- set tid = "home-meeting-title" if dark else "home-meeting-title-2" -%}
{%- set hTag = "p" if dark else "h2" -%}
{#- where it is held ("Join on Zoom") and who may come, for the calendar entry: config/site.yml meeting.platform, note -#}
{%- set pf = { platform: mt.platform or "Zoom" } -%}
{%- set mNote = mt | pick(L, "note") -%}
{%- set sp = meeting.next.speaker -%}
{%- set spTopic = (sp.topic[L] or sp.topic.en) if sp else "" -%}
{%- set spList = [] -%}
{%- for s in spk.list %}{% set _n = spList.push({ ymd: s.ymd, name: s.name, topic: s.topic }) %}{% endfor -%}
<div class="home-meet home-meet--{{ v }}" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{ tid }}"
     x-data="homeMeeting" data-rule="{{ meeting.rule | json }}" data-start="{{ meeting.next.start }}" data-end="{{ meeting.next.end }}"
     data-speakers="{{ spList | json }}" data-speaker-tpl="{{ 'committee.meeting.speaker' | t(L) }}"
     data-cal-title="{{ 'home.meeting_cal_title' | t(L) }}" data-cal-desc="{{ 'home.meeting_cal_desc' | t(L, pf) }}{{ (' ' + mNote) if mNote }}" data-cal-loc="{{ mt.online_url }}"
     data-cal-url="{{ '/meetings/#committee-meeting' | lurl(L) | siteUrl(site) }}">
  <div class="home-meet-info">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
      <{{ hTag }} id="{{ tid }}" class="home-meet-eyebrow">{{ "home.meeting_eyebrow" | t(L) }}</{{ hTag }}>
      {#- "Happening now — come on in!": written by the browser while the meeting is on (never in the HTML: a crawler
          that runs no script would read it as true — since round 35; app.js GV.say says more) -#}
      <span x-show="live" x-cloak class="home-live-pill" data-gv-say="{{ 'home.meeting_live' | t(L) }}" x-text="live ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''"></span>
    </div>
    <p class="home-meet-date" x-ref="date" x-text="dateLabel">{{ meeting.next.start | homeMeetingDate(L) }}</p>
    <p class="home-meet-time">
      {% icon "clock", "size-4 shrink-0" %}<span x-ref="time" x-text="timeLabel">{{ meeting.next.start | homeTimeRange(meeting.next.end, L) }}</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>{{ mt.platform or "Zoom" }}</span>
    </p>
    {% if not dark and meeting.rule and meeting.rule.n %}
    <p class="home-meet-rule">{{ "home.meeting_rule" | t(L, { nth: ("home.nth." ~ meeting.rule.n) | t(L), weekday: meeting.rule.weekday | homeWeekday(L) }) }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {#- that date's guest speaker: "Guest speaker: Rick W.", the topic under it (one line at most in the hero, two
        below it; the whole of it is on /meetings/) -#}
    {% if spList | length %}
    <p class="mt-2 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm leading-snug {{ 'text-white/85' if dark else 'text-muted' }}" x-show="speaker"{% if not sp %} x-cloak{% endif %}>
      {% icon "mic", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0" %}
      <span class="min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold {{ 'text-white' if dark else 'text-ink' }}" x-text="speakerLine">{{ ("committee.meeting.speaker" | t(L, { name: sp.name })) if sp }}</span>
        <span class="{{ 'line-clamp-1' if dark else 'line-clamp-2' }}" x-show="speaker && speaker.topic"{% if not spTopic %} x-cloak{% endif %}>“<span x-text="speaker ? speaker.topic : ''">{{ spTopic }}</span>”</span></span>
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="home-meet-count" role="timer" aria-label="{{ 'home.countdown_aria' | t(L) }}" x-show="!live">
    {% for u in [["d", "common.days"], ["h", "common.hours"], ["m", "common.min"], ["s", "common.sec"]] %}
    <div class="home-count"><span class="home-count-n" x-text="pad({{ u[0] }})">--</span><span class="home-count-l">{{ u[1] | t(L) }}</span></div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="home-meet-actions">
    <a class="{{ 'btn-light' if dark else 'btn-primary' }} home-meet-join" href="{{ mt.online_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ "home.meeting_join" | t(L, pf) }}<span class="sr-only"> {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>
    <button type="button" class="{{ 'btn-on-dark' if dark else 'btn-secondary' }} btn-sm" x-show="ready" x-cloak @click="addToCalendar()" title="{{ 'common.add_to_calendar' | t(L) }}">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} {{ "home.meeting_add_cal" | t(L) }}</button>
    <a class="{{ 'btn-on-dark' if dark else 'btn-secondary' }} btn-sm home-meet-more" href="{{ '/meetings/' | lurl(L) }}#committee-meeting">{{ "home.meeting_details_short" | t(L) }} {% icon "arrow-right", "size-3.5" %}<span class="sr-only"> — {{ "home.meeting_eyebrow" | t(L) }}</span></a>
  </div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{#- Compact "next Grapevine Meeting" card (round 30): our monthly online Grapevine Meeting, right under the
    committee meeting's card — in the hero from 1024px (v = "hero", dark glass) and below the hero on smaller
    screens (v = "page", a light card); only one of the two is ever displayed, so each has its own heading id (an
    <h2> below the hero only, as the committee card's). gm = site | cmSeriesNext("grapevine-meeting", L,
    D.events.items) (eleventy/filters/committee.js seriesNext: worked out from the settings, config/site.yml
    recurring_events, with the same dates and words as /meetings/#grapevine-meeting and /events/); without it the
    card is left out. The eyebrow "Next Grapevine Meeting" with "Happening now" during the meeting, "First meeting"
    on its first date (`starts`) and, on /es/, "En inglés"; the date and time in one line; then Join (its accessible
    name names the meeting: both of our meetings use the same room) and Details → /meetings/#grapevine-meeting
    (class home-gvm-more: home-meet-more and data-cal-url belong to the committee meeting's card). No countdown
    tiles and no Add to calendar here: the meeting's section on /meetings/ has both. The browser rolls the date on
    as the committee card's does (home.js homeMeeting with the series' rule — `starts` in data-rule — and
    data-first for "First meeting"). -#}
{% macro gvmCard(v, L, gm) %}
{%- set dark = v == "hero" -%}
{%- set tid = "home-gvm-title" if dark else "home-gvm-title-2" -%}
{%- set hTag = "p" if dark else "h2" -%}
{%- set isFirst = gm.starts and gm.next.startYmd == gm.starts -%}
{%- set gmPf = { platform: gm.join.platform } -%}
<div class="home-gvm home-gvm--{{ v }}" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{ tid }}"
     x-data="homeMeeting" data-rule="{{ gm.rule | json }}" data-start="{{ gm.next.startIso }}" data-end="{{ gm.next.endIso }}" data-first="{{ gm.starts }}">
  <div class="home-gvm-info">
    <div class="home-gvm-head">
      <{{ hTag }} id="{{ tid }}" class="home-meet-eyebrow">{{ "home.gvm_eyebrow" | t(L) }}</{{ hTag }}>
      <span class="home-gvm-pills">
        {#- (both pills' words are in the HTML only while they are true: "Happening now" never, "First meeting" on its
            first date — the browser writes them in when they become true: data-gv-say, since round 35) -#}
        <span x-show="live" x-cloak class="home-live-pill" data-gv-say="{{ 'home.meeting_live' | t(L) }}" x-text="live ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''"></span>
        <span x-show="isFirst && !live" class="home-gvm-pill"{% if not isFirst %} x-cloak{% endif %} data-gv-say="{{ 'committee.meeting.first' | t(L) }}" x-text="isFirst && !live ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''">{{ ("committee.meeting.first" | t(L)) if isFirst }}</span>
        {% if L != "en" %}<span class="home-gvm-pill">{{ "committee.weekly.lang_en" | t(L) }}</span>{% endif %}
      </span>
    </div>
    <p class="home-gvm-when"><span class="home-gvm-row"><span class="home-gvm-date" x-ref="date" x-text="dateLabel">{{ gm.next.startIso | homeMeetingDate(L) }}</span>
      <span class="home-gvm-time"><span x-ref="time" x-text="timeLabel">{{ gm.next.startIso | homeTimeRange(gm.next.endIso, L) }}</span></span></span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="home-gvm-actions">
    {% if gm.join.url %}<a class="{{ 'btn-light' if dark else 'btn-primary' }} btn-sm home-gvm-join" href="{{ gm.join.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ ("home.meeting_join" | t(L, gmPf)) if gm.join.platform else ("committee.events.join_online" | t(L)) }}<span class="sr-only"> — {{ gm.title }} {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>{% endif %}
    <a class="{{ 'btn-on-dark' if dark else 'btn-secondary' }} btn-sm home-gvm-more" href="{{ '/meetings/' | lurl(L) }}#grapevine-meeting">{{ "home.meeting_details_short" | t(L) }} {% icon "arrow-right", "size-3.5" %}<span class="sr-only"> — {{ "home.gvm_eyebrow" | t(L) }}</span></a>
  </div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

{#- One magazine column (Grapevine = blue, La Viña = amber): the current cover + its three newest stories (the
    rest of the issue is one tap away: "All N stories" → /read/). -#}
{% macro magColumn(pub, issue, L, site) %}
{%- set isLv = pub == "lv" -%}
{%- set mag = "La Viña" if isLv else "Grapevine" -%}
{%- set src = site.sources.lavina if isLv else site.sources.grapevine -%}
{%- set hub = src.base + src.magazine_hub -%}
{%- set issueUrl = issue.url or hub -%}
{%- set label = issue.label | homeIssueLabel(L) -%}
{#- Every story shown is machine-translated from one language: say so once, not on each row. -#}
{%- set mtFrom = issue.items | homeAllMachine(L) -%}
<article class="card home-mag flex flex-col overflow-hidden" aria-labelledby="mag-{{ pub }}-title">
  <header class="home-mag-head home-tone-{{ pub }} relative overflow-hidden px-5 pt-6 pb-6 sm:px-8 sm:pt-7">
    {% if not issue.cover %}<svg class="home-mag-grapes" viewBox="0 0 120 120" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="currentColor"><circle cx="46" cy="52" r="11"/><circle cx="68" cy="52" r="11"/><circle cx="57" cy="70" r="11"/><circle cx="35" cy="70" r="11"/><circle cx="79" cy="70" r="11"/><circle cx="46" cy="88" r="11"/><circle cx="68" cy="88" r="11"/><circle cx="57" cy="106" r="11"/></g><path d="M57 40 C 58 26, 66 16, 80 12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>{% endif %}
    {#- The cover floats right, so on narrow screens the chips flow underneath it. It is at most 128 px wide
        (home.css .home-mag-cover: 84–128 px), so it shows the sync's 256 px list copy of the cover when there is
        one (cmListThumb: "<name>.sm.webp" next to the 480 px file, else that file, unchanged). -#}
    <div class="relative flow-root">
      {% if issue.cover %}
      <a href="{{ issueUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="home-mag-cover float-right mb-2 ml-4 sm:ml-6">
        <img src="{{ issue.cover | cmListThumb }}" alt="{{ 'home.cover_alt' | t(L, { mag: mag, label: label }) }}" width="480" height="686" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" onerror="this.parentElement.remove()">
      </a>
      {% endif %}
      <p class="home-mag-tagline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em]">{{ ("home.lv_tagline" if isLv else "home.gv_tagline") | t(L) }}</p>
      <h3 id="mag-{{ pub }}-title" class="mt-1 font-display text-4xl font-semibold italic sm:text-[2.6rem] md:max-lg:text-3xl"{% if isLv and L != "es" %} lang="es"{% endif %}>{{ mag }}</h3>
      {% if issue.label %}
      {#- Inline chips (not flex) so they can wrap around / below the floated cover. -#}
      <p class="mt-4 -mb-2 text-sm font-semibold">
        <span class="home-mag-chip bg-surface/80 shadow-sm">{% icon "book-open-text", "size-4 shrink-0" %} <span>{{ "home.issue_label" | t(L, { label: label }) }}</span></span>
        {% if issue.topic %}<span class="home-mag-chip bg-surface/60"><span>{{ "home.issue_theme" | t(L) }} <span class="italic"{% if issue.topicLang %} lang="{{ issue.topicLang }}"{% endif %}>{{ issue.topic }}</span></span></span>{% endif %}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>
  {% if issue.items.length %}
  {% if mtFrom %}<p class="home-mag-mt flex items-center gap-1.5 border-b border-line px-5 py-2.5 text-xs text-muted sm:px-8">{% icon "languages", "size-3.5 shrink-0" %} {{ ("home.mag_mt_from_" ~ mtFrom) | t(L) }}</p>{% endif %}
  <ol class="flex-1 divide-y divide-line" role="list">
    {% for a in issue.items %}
    {%- set sum = a | tx("summary", L) -%}
    {%- set ttl = a | tx("title", L) -%}
    {%- set sec = a | tx("section", L) -%}
    {%- set freeFlag = a.extra.free if a.extra else "" -%}
    <li class="group relative px-5 py-4 transition hover:bg-surface-2/60 sm:px-8">
      {% if sec %}<p class="text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] {{ 'text-lv' if isLv else 'text-gv' }}"{% if a.lang and a.lang != L and sec == a.extra.section %} lang="{{ a.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ sec }}</p>{% endif %}
      <h4 class="mt-0.5 font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink"{% if a.lang and a.lang != L and ttl == a.title %} lang="{{ a.lang }}"{% endif %}>
        <a href="{{ a.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="no-underline after:absolute after:inset-0 {{ 'group-hover:text-lv' if isLv else 'group-hover:text-gv' }}">{{ ttl }}</a>
        <span class="inline-block align-middle text-faint">{% icon "arrow-up-right", "size-4" %}</span>
      </h4>
      {#- the summary from 640px only: a phone shows the titles, so the page stays short -#}
      {% if sum %}<p class="mt-1 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted max-sm:hidden">{{ sum | excerpt(190) }}</p>{% endif %}
      {% if freeFlag === true or freeFlag === false or (not mtFrom and ((a | machineFor(L)) or (a.lang and a.lang != L))) %}
      <p class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1 text-xs text-faint">
        {% if freeFlag === true %}<span class="badge-vine">{% icon "lock-open", "size-3" %} {{ "home.free_read" | t(L) }}</span>{% elif freeFlag === false %}<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-medium" title="{{ 'home.subscriber_help' | t(L) }}">{% icon "lock", "size-3" %} {{ "home.subscriber_only" | t(L) }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if not mtFrom %}{{ ui.langPill(a, L) }}{{ ui.autoNote(a, L) }}{% endif %}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% else %}
  <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 py-10 text-center sm:px-8">
    <span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-surface-2 text-faint">{% icon "book-open-text", "size-6" %}</span>
    <p class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ "home.mag_empty_title" | t(L) }}</p>
    <p class="max-w-sm text-sm text-muted">{{ ("home.mag_empty_lv" if isLv else "home.mag_empty_gv") | t(L) }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <footer class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-line px-5 py-5 sm:px-8">
    <a class="{{ 'btn-lv' if isLv else 'btn-primary' }}" href="{{ issueUrl if issue.items.length else hub }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "book-open", "size-4" %} {{ ("home.read_issue" if issue.items.length else "home.visit_site") | t(L) }}<span class="sr-only"> {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>
    {% if issue.total > 3 %}<a href="{{ ('/read/#' ~ pub ~ '-current') | lurl(L) }}" class="btn-secondary btn-sm ml-auto">{{ "home.issue_count" | t(L, { n: issue.total }) }} {% icon "arrow-right", "size-4" %}</a>{% endif %}
  </footer>
</article>
{% endmacro %}

{#- =====================================================================
    1. HERO — the shared page hero (ui.pageHero: the committee's animated grapevine art) · headline, lead and two
       buttons: "Find an AA meeting near you" (AA's own meeting finder, in the page language: config/site.yml
       links.aa_find / aa_find_es — the same link as the "New to AA?" card's) and "See what's new" · from 1024px our
       two monthly meetings on the right, one card under the other (.home-meets): the next committee meeting's
       (meetingCard, with its countdown — always the first) and the next Grapevine Meeting's (gvmCard, compact).
       With both the Home hero is TALLER than every other page's 30rem (480px), the minimum ui.pageHero keeps: the
       hero grows to fit its right column (about 590–640px at 1280px and wider, 640–685 at 1024px). Below 1024px
       both cards are the first block under the hero, so the hero keeps its standard height there.
    ===================================================================== -#}
{%- set mt = site.meeting -%}
{#- the guest speakers to come (the next-meeting card: each date's, once it rolls on) -#}
{%- set spk = site | cmSpeakers(L) -%}
{#- our monthly Grapevine Meeting (config/site.yml recurring_events "grapevine-meeting"), from the settings; null
    without a date to come (its card is then left out) -#}
{%- set gm = site | cmSeriesNext("grapevine-meeting", L, D.events.items) -%}
{%- set findAA = site.links | langLink("aa_find", L) -%}
{% call(slot) ui.pageHero(L, ("home.hero_title" | t(L)) | mdInline | safe, ("home.hero_lead" | t(L)) | gloss(L), "", "home.hero_eyebrow" | t(L), { id: "homeHero", titleId: "home-title", aside: true, eyebrowIcon: "grapes" }) %}
  {%- if slot == "aside" %}
  {% if meeting.next or gm %}
  <div class="home-meets">
    {% if meeting.next %}{{ meetingCard("hero", L, meeting, mt, spk) }}{% endif %}
    {% if gm %}{{ gvmCard("hero", L, gm) }}{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {%- else %}
  <div class="hero-actions home-hero-actions">
    {% if findAA %}<a class="btn-light home-find-aa" href="{{ findAA }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "map-pin", "size-4" %} {{ "home.cta_find_aa" | t(L) }}<span class="sr-only"> {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>{% endif %}
    <a class="{{ 'btn-on-dark' if findAA else 'btn-light' }}" href="{{ '/whats-new/' | lurl(L) }}">{% icon "sparkles", "size-4" %} {{ "home.cta_whats_new" | t(L) }}</a>
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
{% endcall %}

{#- =====================================================================
    2. UNDER THE HERO, tucked into its faded edge (page-overlap): below 1024px our two meeting cards (from 1024px
       both are in the hero); then "Where would you like to start?" — four big buttons, each to the page that does
       that best:
         · I'm new to AA → the "New to AA?" first-steps card on /meetings/#new-to-aa (AA's own finder, "Is AA for
           you?", the Meeting Guide app, the AA offices in our Area) — Home's one link there;
         · I'm a group rep (GVR / RLV) → the GVR / RLV corner (/gvr/);
         · I want to write my story → Share your story (/contribute/), with the next story deadline of either
           magazine when there is one (homeThemes' first dated theme; it hides itself once its day is over);
         · I want to subscribe → the Shop's subscriptions (/shop/#subscriptions), "from $… a month" when the
           stores' prices are known (shopFromMonthly).
       Two columns from 640px, four in a row from 1280px.
    3. THE DAILY QUOTE (db.quote ← scripts/sync/quote.py; homeDailyQuotes): Grapevine's Daily Quote and La Viña's
       Cita Diaria exactly as published, each in its own language (lang set, never translated), the page language's
       magazine first — side by side from 1024px, stacked below; on phones (< 640px, with JS) only the page
       language's quote, the other behind one button. Each quote shows ITS day; home.js adds "Today" /
       "Yesterday" in the visitor's browser (Central time) and, for a quote that is not today's, names the link
       "Today's quote on …". Links: the quote on the official home page and the official e-mail sign-up. Under both
       quotes, once for the card, the publishers' permission credits in their own wording. Left out when there is
       no quote from the last 2 days (two runs a day keep it current).
    ===================================================================== -#}
{%- set quotes = D.quote | homeDailyQuotes(L, 2) -%}
{#- (homeThemes lists the dated themes first, soonest first: the first one, when it has a deadline, is the next) -#}
{%- set themes = D.editorial.items | homeThemes(4) -%}
{%- set nextTheme = themes[0] if (themes.length and themes[0].extra.deadline) else null -%}
{%- set subsFrom = db.shop | shopFromMonthly -%}
{%- set choices = [
  { key: "new", url: "/meetings/#new-to-aa", icon: "hand-heart", tone: "vine", text: "newcomer.line" | t(L) },
  { key: "rep", url: "/gvr/", icon: "badge-check", tone: "gv", text: "home.choose_rep_text" | t(L) },
  { key: "write", url: "/contribute/", icon: "feather", tone: "grape", text: "home.choose_write_text" | t(L) },
  { key: "sub", url: "/shop/#subscriptions", icon: "newspaper", tone: "lv",
    text: ("shop.subs_from" | t(L, { amount: subsFrom | shopMoney(L) })) if subsFrom else ("home.subs_desc" | t(L)) }
] -%}
<div class="container-page page-overlap home-under">
  {% if meeting.next or gm %}
  <div class="card home-under-card lg:hidden">
    {% if meeting.next %}<div class="home-under-meet">{{ meetingCard("page", L, meeting, mt, spk) }}</div>{% endif %}
    {% if gm %}<div class="home-under-gvm">{{ gvmCard("page", L, gm) }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="card home-choose" aria-labelledby="choose-title">
    <h2 id="choose-title" class="home-choose-title">{{ "home.choose_title" | t(L) }}</h2>
    <ul class="home-choose-grid" role="list">
      {% for c in choices %}
      <li>
        <a class="home-choose-btn home-tone-{{ c.tone }} group" href="{{ c.url | lurl(L) }}">
          <span class="home-choose-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon c.icon, "size-6" %}</span>
          <span class="home-choose-body">
            <span class="home-choose-label"><span class="home-choose-go" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "arrow-right", "size-5" %}</span>{{ ("home.choose_" ~ c.key) | t(L) }}</span>
            <span class="home-choose-text">{{ c.text }}</span>
            {%- if c.key == "write" and nextTheme %}
            {%- set thIsLv = nextTheme.extra.publication == "lv" %}
            <span class="home-choose-due" data-gv-expire="{{ nextTheme.extra.deadline | fsDayEnd }}">{% icon "calendar-clock", "size-3.5 shrink-0" %} {{ "home.choose_write_next" | t(L, { date: nextTheme.extra.deadline | fmtDate(L, "short"), mag: "La Viña" if thIsLv else "Grapevine" }) }}</span>
            {%- endif %}
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  {#- Pinned on the Bulletin: the committee's pinned posts (two at most), only while one is on — its title, one line of
      it and "Read" to the post on /bulletin/; each goes at the end of its last day (data-gv-expire: app.js), and the
      card with the last one (data-gv-expire-list). No pinned post: no card, and the page stays as short. -#}
  {%- set pins = (D.announcements.items | cmAnnouncements) | selectattr("_pinned") | limit(2) -%}
  {% if pins.length %}
  <section class="card home-pins" aria-labelledby="pins-title" data-gv-expire-list>
    <h2 id="pins-title" class="home-pins-title">{% icon "pin", "size-4 shrink-0" %} {{ "home.pins_title" | t(L) }}</h2>
    <ul class="home-pins-list" role="list">
      {% for a in pins %}
      {%- set pinTitle = a | tx("title", L) -%}
      {%- set pinText = (a | tx("summary", L)) | excerpt(160) -%}
      {%- set pinEnd = (a.extra.expires | fsDayEnd) if (a.extra and a.extra.expires) else "" -%}
      <li class="home-pin" data-gv-expire-item{% if pinEnd %} data-gv-expire="{{ pinEnd }}"{% endif %}>
        <div class="home-pin-body">
          {#- a title the translation left as it was is in the post's own language (as on /bulletin/) -#}
          <h3 class="home-pin-title"{% if a.lang and a.lang != L and pinTitle == a.title %} lang="{{ a.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ pinTitle }}</h3>
          {% if pinText %}<p class="home-pin-text">{{ ui.autoNote(a, L) }}{{ " " if (a | machineFor(L)) }}{{ pinText }}</p>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <a class="home-pin-read link tap-link" href="{{ (a.url if (a.url and a.url.startsWith('/bulletin/')) else '/bulletin/#' + a._anchor) | lurl(L) }}">{{ "home.pins_read" | t(L) }}<span class="sr-only">: {{ pinTitle }}</span> {% icon "arrow-right", "size-4 shrink-0" %}</a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if quotes.length %}
  <section class="card home-quote" aria-labelledby="quote-title">
    <h2 id="quote-title" class="home-quote-title">{% icon "quote", "size-4 shrink-0" %} {{ "home.quote_title" | t(L) }}</h2>
    <div class="home-quote-grid{{ ' is-single' if quotes.length == 1 }}" data-quote-grid>
      {% for q in quotes %}
      {%- set isLv = q.pub == "lv" -%}
      {%- set mag = "La Viña" if isLv else "Grapevine" -%}
      {% if not loop.first %}
      <button type="button" class="home-q-toggle btn-ghost btn-sm" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="quote-{{ q.pub }}" data-quote-toggle>{% icon "chevron-down", "size-4 shrink-0" %}<span>{{ ("home.quote_show_" ~ q.pub) | t(L) }}</span></button>
      {% endif %}
      <article id="quote-{{ q.pub }}" class="home-q home-tone-{{ q.pub }}{{ ' is-other' if not loop.first }}" aria-labelledby="quote-{{ q.pub }}-mag" data-quote-day="{{ q.date }}">
        <div class="home-q-head">
          <h3 id="quote-{{ q.pub }}-mag" class="home-q-mag"{% if isLv and L != "es" %} lang="es"{% endif %}>{{ mag }}</h3>
          {#- "Today" / "Yesterday": only the browser knows (home.js markQuoteToday), so their words wait in data-gv-say
              (never in the HTML, where a crawler read "Today Yesterday" before the date — since round 35) -#}
          <p class="home-q-when"><span class="badge-new" data-quote-today hidden data-gv-say="{{ 'home.quote_today' | t(L) }}"></span><span class="badge-muted" data-quote-yesterday hidden data-gv-say="{{ 'home.quote_yesterday' | t(L) }}"></span><time datetime="{{ q.date }}">{{ q.day }}</time></p>
          {% if q.lang != L %}<span class="badge-muted"><span class="uppercase" aria-hidden="true">{{ q.lang }}</span><span class="sr-only">{{ ('lang.' ~ q.lang) | t(L) }}</span></span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <figure class="home-q-fig">
          <blockquote class="home-q-text" lang="{{ q.lang }}" cite="{{ q.url }}"><p>{{ q.text }}</p></blockquote>
          {% if q.attribution or q.source %}
          <figcaption class="home-q-by">
            {% if q.attribution %}<span class="block" lang="{{ q.lang }}">— {{ q.attribution }}</span>{% endif %}
            {% if q.source %}<span class="block">{{ "home.quote_from" | t(L) }} <cite{% if (q.source_lang or q.lang) != L %} lang="{{ q.source_lang or q.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ q.source }}</cite></span>{% endif %}
          </figcaption>
          {% endif %}
        </figure>
        <p class="home-q-links">
          {#- the link's name: "Read it on …" (the build's quote is the day's) or "Today's quote on …"; the other one's
              words wait in data-gv-say for home.js -#}
          {%- set qThis = "home.quote_more" | t(L, { host: q.host }) %}
          {%- set qToday = "home.quote_today_on" | t(L, { host: q.host }) %}
          <a class="link tap-link" href="{{ q.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-quote-link="this"{% if not q.fresh %} hidden{% endif %} data-gv-say="{{ qThis }}">{{ qThis if q.fresh }}</span><span data-quote-link="today"{% if q.fresh %} hidden{% endif %} data-gv-say="{{ qToday }}">{{ qToday if not q.fresh }}</span><span class="sr-only"> {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>
          {% if q.signup_url %}<a class="link tap-link" href="{{ q.signup_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "mail", "size-4 shrink-0" %}{{ "home.quote_email" | t(L) }}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ mag }}) {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>{% endif %}
        </p>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {#- the publishers' permission credits, in their own wording: once, under the quotes (outside the grid, so
        the phone's one quote keeps them whichever quote shows) -#}
    <p class="home-quote-rights">{{ "home.quote_credit_aaws" | t(L) }}&nbsp;<span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ "home.quote_credit_gv" | t(L) }}</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{#- =====================================================================
    4. FROM THE MAGAZINES — the latest Grapevine + La Viña issues side by side from 768px (La Viña first on /es/),
       three stories each (the whole issue is on /read/ and on the magazine's site). Under them: this month's Book of
       the Month while the stores' offer is on (assets/js/shop.js keeps "N days left" current and swaps the line once
       it has ended; the Shop page is the ONE home of the prices and dates), and one line to the story themes and
       deadlines (/contribute/#deadlines) and the deadlines calendar (/contribute/#deadlines-calendar — only while a
       dated deadline is open: that section of /contribute/ is left out otherwise, as the calendar is empty).
    ===================================================================== -#}
{%- set dlCalOpen = db | mpDeadlineCals(site, L) | length -%}
{%- set gvIssue = D.articles.items | homeLatestIssue("gv", 3, D.articles.issues, L) -%}
{%- set lvIssue = D.articles.items | homeLatestIssue("lv", 3, D.articles.issues, L) -%}
{%- set magOrder = ["lv", "gv"] if L == "es" else ["gv", "lv"] -%}
{%- set hBotm = db.shop | shopBotm(L) -%}
{%- set shopHref = "/shop/" | lurl(L) -%}
{%- set hSoon = null -%}
{%- set hFirst = null -%}
{%- set hEnds = [] -%}
{#- the card runs until the LAST offer ends (hSoon); its "N days left" counts to the FIRST one still running (hFirst:
    Grapevine's and La Viña's offers can end on different days — shop.js moves on to the next one, data-shop-ends) -#}
{%- for b in hBotm %}{% if b.ends %}{% set _he = hEnds.push(b.ends) %}{% if not hSoon or b.ends > hSoon.ends %}{% set hSoon = b %}{% endif %}{% if not hFirst or b.ends < hFirst.ends %}{% set hFirst = b %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set hPct = hBotm[0].pct if (hBotm.length and (hBotm.length == 1 or hBotm[0].pct == hBotm[1].pct)) else 0 -%}
<section class="section section-band mt-6" aria-labelledby="mag-title">
  <div class="container-page">
    {{ ui.sectionHead("home.mag_title" | t(L), "home.mag_sub" | t(L), "/read/" | lurl(L), "home.mag_all" | t(L), "book-open", { eyebrow: "home.mag_eyebrow" | t(L), tone: "text-gv", id: "mag-title", lang: L }) }}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      {% for pub in magOrder %}{{ magColumn(pub, lvIssue if pub == "lv" else gvIssue, L, site) }}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="home-mag-more mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4{{ ' lg:grid-cols-2' if hBotm.length }}">
      {% if hBotm.length %}
      <a class="shop-teaser card card-link group flex h-full items-center gap-4 p-4 no-underline" href="{{ shopHref }}#botm" data-shop-offer{% if hSoon %} data-ends="{{ hSoon.ends }}"{% endif %}>
        <span class="shop-teaser-covers" aria-hidden="true">{% for b in hBotm %}{% if b.image %}<img src="{{ b.image | cmListThumb }}" alt="" width="389" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>
        <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
          <span class="eyebrow flex items-center gap-1.5 text-lv">{% icon "badge-percent", "size-4 shrink-0" %} {{ "shop.botm_title" | t(L) }}</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-balance text-ink group-hover:text-lv">{% if hPct %}<span data-shop-live>{{ "home.botm_title" | t(L, { pct: hPct }) }}</span><span data-shop-ended hidden>{{ "shop.botm_title" | t(L) }}</span>{% else %}{{ "home.botm_title_plain" | t(L) }}{% endif %}</span>
          {% if hFirst and hFirst.days !== null %}<span class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted" data-shop-live><span data-shop-days data-lastmod="skip" class="shop-days{{ ' is-urgent' if hFirst.days <= 3 }}" data-shop-ends="{{ hEnds | sort | join(' ') }}" data-t-many="{{ 'shop.days_left' | t(L) }}" data-t-tomorrow="{{ 'shop.ends_tomorrow' | t(L) }}" data-t-last="{{ 'shop.last_day' | t(L) }}">{% if hFirst.days === 0 %}{{ "shop.last_day" | t(L) }}{% elif hFirst.days === 1 %}{{ "shop.ends_tomorrow" | t(L) }}{% else %}{{ "shop.days_left" | t(L, { n: hFirst.days }) }}{% endif %}</span></span>{% endif %}
        </span>
        <span class="home-botm-go shrink-0 text-faint transition group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:text-lv" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "arrow-right", "size-4" %}</span>
      </a>
      {% endif %}
      {#- (round 38b) [--text-col-min:9em]: at relaxed spacing and 130 %+ main.css's text-column rule lets the title
          shrink to 7em beside "Upcoming themes and deadlines" — at 462–479px with relaxed spacing (100 %) that was
          101–116px, and "magazines" with its icon needs 117px there: it broke in two. 9em is 126px there; with less
          beside the link the title has a line of its own. (Measured in Chrome at every width from 320 to 1440px, both
          languages, relaxed spacing and 130–150 %: no word broken; 8em still broke it at 477–479px. 15rem, its
          basis-60, would have made the line taller at 483 of those settings, 9em at 62 — by 11–43px — and shorter at
          107.) -#}
      <p class="home-write-line panel-muted flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-sm">
        <span class="inline-flex min-w-0 flex-1 basis-60 items-center gap-2 font-semibold text-ink [--text-col-min:9em]"><span class="text-grape">{% icon "pen-line", "size-5 shrink-0" %}</span>{{ "home.write_title" | t(L) }}</span>
        <a class="link tap-link" href="{{ '/contribute/#deadlines' | lurl(L) }}">{{ "home.write_themes" | t(L) }}</a>
        {% if dlCalOpen %}
        <a class="link tap-link inline-flex items-center gap-1.5" href="{{ '/contribute/#deadlines-calendar' | lurl(L) }}">{% icon "calendar-sync", "size-4 shrink-0" %} {{ "home.write_dlcal" | t(L) }}</a>
        {% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- =====================================================================
    5. LISTEN & WATCH — the featured podcast episode (it plays right here: homePlayer, with Listen's saved places)
       beside "More episodes" (the next three — two on phones —, each with a play button that loads it into the
       episode card's player; under them both weekly open meetings in one line, details on /meetings/#weekly-open),
       then the newest YouTube video as one compact strip under the two cards: a small 16:9 lite-youtube (it plays
       right there, privacy-enhanced) beside its badges, its title (two lines at most), date and length, and
       "Subscribe on YouTube" (from 640px; on phones "All videos" in the section's head is the way on). The strip's
       video is never the YouTube copy of an episode shown above (homeVideos skips them, as the videos row did
       before November 2026). Every episode is on /listen/, every video on /watch/. Left out when there are neither;
       without episodes the strip is the section, without a video the two cards are.
    ===================================================================== -#}
{%- set epPick = D.episodes.items | homeEpisodes(D.episodes.shows or site.sources.podcasts) -%}
{%- set ep = epPick.featured -%}
{%- set moreEps = epPick.more -%}
{%- set vids = D.videos.items | homeVideos(1, ep, moreEps) -%}
{%- set v = vids[0] -%}
{%- set podCfg = (site.sources.podcasts | homeShow(ep)) if ep else {} -%}
{%- set show = (D.episodes.shows | homeShow(ep)) if ep else {} -%}
{%- set pod = {
  apple: (ep.extra.apple if ep else "") or show.apple or podCfg.apple,
  spotify: (ep.extra.spotify if ep else "") or show.spotify or podCfg.spotify,
  amazon: (ep.extra.amazon if ep else "") or show.amazon or podCfg.amazon
} -%}
{% set wo = D.weekly_open.items[0] %}
{% if ep or v %}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="lw-title">
  <div class="container-page">
    {% call ui.sectionHead("home.lw_title" | t(L), "home.lw_sub" | t(L), ("/listen/" | lurl(L)) if ep else ("/watch/" | lurl(L)), ("home.all_episodes" if ep else "home.all_videos") | t(L), "headphones", { eyebrow: "home.lw_eyebrow" | t(L), tone: "text-grape", id: "lw-title", lang: L }) %}
    {% if ep and v %}<a href="{{ '/watch/' | lurl(L) }}" class="btn-ghost btn-sm">{% icon "circle-play", "size-4" %} {{ "home.all_videos" | t(L) }}</a>{% endif %}
    {% endcall %}
    {% if ep %}
    {%- set epShow = ep | mediaShowOf(epShows) -%}
    {%- set epTitle = ep | mediaTitle(L) -%}
    {%- set epSE = ep | mediaSE(L) -%}
    {#- A weekly open meeting's title that names the meeting's date ("Meeting of September 16, 2026") needs no date
        of its own; one without it ("<show name>, episode 3") keeps the date. -#}
    {%- set epMeta = ([ep.extra.duration_sec | duration] if (ep | mediaTitleDated(L)) else [ep.date | fmtDate(L, "medium"), ep.extra.duration_sec | duration]) | join(" · ") -%}
    {#- With shows in both languages (La Viña's open meeting is in Spanish), an episode in the other language says so,
        as on /listen/ (ui.langPill: "ES" / "EN") -#}
    {%- set epMixed = (epShows | where("lang", "es")).length and (epShows | where("lang", "en")).length -%}
    {#- the weekly open meetings' line: under "More episodes" (its last row); with no more episodes, under the player -#}
    {%- set woLink -%}
    {%- if wo and wo.extra -%}
    {%- set woWhen = D.weekly_open.items | mediaWeeklyDays(L) -%}
    {%- set woMany = D.weekly_open.items.length > 1 -%}
    {#- both weekly open meetings in one line (as on /listen/ and /watch/); details on /meetings/ -#}
    <a href="{{ '/meetings/#weekly-open' | lurl(L) }}" class="home-wo-link group {{ 'mt-auto' if moreEps.length else 'mt-4' }} flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl bg-gv-soft/60 p-3.5 no-underline transition hover:bg-gv-soft">
      <span class="home-wo-icon grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-surface text-gv">{% icon "video", "size-5" %}</span>
      <span class="min-w-0">
        <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-gv">{{ ("home.weekly_opens" if woMany else "home.weekly_open") | t(L) }}</span>
        <span class="block text-xs leading-snug text-muted">{{ ("home.weekly_opens_text" if woMany else "home.weekly_open_text") | t(L, { when: woWhen }) if woWhen else (("home.weekly_opens_fallback" if woMany else "home.weekly_open_fallback") | t(L)) }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="home-wo-go ml-auto self-center text-faint transition group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:text-gv" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "arrow-right", "size-4" %}</span>
    </a>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- endset -%}
    {#- Side by side (from 1024px) the two cards are the same height (the grid stretches them; they stack at 150% text
        below 1280px, home.css .home-lw). Each one's footer is anchored to its bottom (mt-auto): the player in the
        episode card (the extra height of a shorter episode card sits between its text and the player), the weekly
        open meetings link in "More episodes" (there the episode rows share the extra height: the list grows and so
        does each row).
        homePlayer (home.js) is the wrapper's, so the play buttons of "More episodes" drive the episode card's player;
        it keeps Listen's saved places: data-left / data-resume are its "Continue listening" words (data-left after a
        dash, inside the sentence: "— 23 min left" / "— quedan 23 min", not Listen's label) -#}
    <div class="home-lw grid grid-cols-1 gap-6{{ ' lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.45fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]' if moreEps.length }}" x-data="homePlayer"
         data-left="{{ 'media.resume_left' | t(L) }}" data-resume="{{ 'media.resume' | t(L) }}">
      <article class="home-episode card relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden p-5 sm:p-7" aria-labelledby="ep-title">
        <div class="relative mb-5 flex items-start gap-4 sm:gap-5">
          <div class="relative size-20 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-grape-soft shadow-[var(--shadow-card)] sm:size-40">
            <span class="absolute inset-0 grid place-items-center text-grape" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "headphones", "size-10" %}</span>
            {% if ep.extra.thumb or ep.image %}<img x-ref="art" src="{{ ep.extra.thumb or ep.image }}" alt="" width="160" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" class="absolute inset-0 size-full object-cover" onerror="this.style.visibility='hidden'">{% endif %}
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs text-muted">
              <span class="badge-grape" x-show="!current">{% icon "headphones", "size-3" %} {{ "home.latest_episode" | t(L) }}</span>
              {#- the player's states — "Now playing", "Played" (this device), "Continue listening" — are only ever true in a
                  browser: their words are written in by Alpine from data-gv-say, never in the HTML (since round 35) -#}
              <span class="badge-grape" x-show="current" x-cloak>{% icon "audio-lines", "size-3" %} <span data-gv-say="{{ 'home.now_playing' | t(L) }}" x-text="current ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''"></span></span>
              {% if epSE %}<span x-show="!current" class="font-semibold">{{ epSE }}</span>{% endif %}
              {%- set epShowLang = epShow.lang if epShow else "en" -%}
              {% if ep.extra.show_name or show.name %}<span x-show="!current"{% if L != epShowLang %} lang="{{ epShowLang }}"{% endif %}>{{ ep.extra.show_name or show.name }}</span>{% endif %}
              {% if epMixed and ep.lang != L and ep.lang in ["en", "es"] %}<span class="inline-flex" x-show="!current">{{ ui.langPill(ep, L) }}</span>{% endif %}
              <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-semibold text-vine" x-show="!current && isDone('{{ ep.id }}')" x-cloak>{% icon "check", "size-3.5" %}<span data-gv-say="{{ 'media.played' | t(L) }}" x-text="isDone('{{ ep.id }}') ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''"></span></span>
            </p>
            <h3 id="ep-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink sm:text-[1.7rem]" x-ref="title" x-text="title">{{ epTitle }}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-faint" x-ref="meta" x-text="meta">{{ epMeta }}</p>
            {#- the audio file's size — only while Data saver is on (areas/pwa.css .pwa-saver-only) -#}
            {% if ep.extra.audio_bytes %}<p class="pwa-saver-only mt-0.5 text-sm text-faint" x-show="!current"><span class="sr-only">{{ "pwa.audio_size" | t(L) }} </span>{{ ep.extra.audio_bytes | fileSize }}</p>{% endif %}
            {%- set epSum = ep | tx("summary", L) -%}
            {% if epSum %}<p class="mt-3 line-clamp-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted max-sm:hidden lg:line-clamp-4" x-show="!current">{{ epSum | excerpt(300) }}</p>{% endif %}
            {% if ep | machineFor(L) %}<p class="mt-2" x-show="!current">{{ ui.autoNote(ep, L) }}</p>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
        {#- The player sits in the same frame as the Listen page's player (media-player) -#}
        <div class="media-player relative mt-auto">
          {% if ep.extra.audio_url %}
          {#- "Continue listening": the episode last left part-way on this device (here or on /listen/), until
              something plays here (keyboard focus in it then goes to the player: home.js focusPlayer) -#}
          <div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3" x-ref="resume" x-show="resume && !started" x-cloak>
            <p class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm leading-snug text-muted"><span class="font-semibold text-lv-strong" data-gv-say="{{ 'media.continue_listening' | t(L) }}:" x-text="resume ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''"></span>
              <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-text="resume ? resume.t : ''"></span> — <span class="whitespace-nowrap" x-text="resumeLeft()"></span></p>
            <button type="button" class="btn-lv btn-sm shrink-0" @click="resumeLast()" :aria-label="resumeLabel()">{% icon "play", "size-4" %}{{ "media.resume" | t(L) }}</button>
          </div>
          {%- set epArt = ep.extra.thumb or ep.image -%}
          <audio x-ref="audio" class="home-audio w-full" controls preload="none" src="{{ ep.extra.audio_url }}"
                 data-id="{{ ep.id }}" data-src="{{ ep.extra.audio_url }}" data-title="{{ epTitle }}" data-img="{{ (epArt | url) if epArt else '' }}"
                 data-du="{{ ep.extra.duration_sec or '' }}" data-sh="{{ ep.extra.show or ep.category or 'gv' }}" data-u="{{ ep | mediaEpisodePage }}">
            {{ "home.audio_fallback" | t(L) }} <a href="{{ ep.extra.audio_url }}">{{ "home.download_episode" | t(L) }}</a>.
          </audio>
          {% endif %}
          {% if pod.apple or pod.spotify or pod.amazon %}
          {#- one line: it scrolls sideways on phones, wraps from 1024px -#}
          <div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2{{ ' mt-3' if ep.extra.audio_url }}">
            <span class="shrink-0 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-faint">{{ "home.listen_on" | t(L) }}</span>
            <div class="chip-row flex-1">
              {% if pod.apple %}<a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ pod.apple }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "podcast", "size-4" %} Apple Podcasts</a>{% endif %}
              {% if pod.spotify %}<a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ pod.spotify }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "spotify", "size-4" %} Spotify</a>{% endif %}
              {% if pod.amazon %}<a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ pod.amazon }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "music", "size-4" %} Amazon Music</a>{% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if not moreEps.length %}{{ woLink | safe }}{% endif %}
        </div>
      </article>

      {% if moreEps.length %}
      <div class="home-more-eps card card-pad flex flex-col">
        <h3 class="card-h"><span class="text-grape!">{% icon "list-music", "size-5" %}</span>{{ "home.more_episodes" | t(L) }}</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 flex grow flex-col divide-y divide-line{{ ' mb-3' if (wo and wo.extra) }}" role="list">
          {% for e in moreEps %}
          {%- set et = e | mediaTitle(L) -%}
          {%- set eShow = e | mediaShowOf(epShows) -%}
          {#- A weekly open meeting's title that names its date ("Meeting of …"): then the meta line skips the date. -#}
          {%- set em = ([e.extra.duration_sec | duration] if (e | mediaTitleDated(L)) else [e.date | fmtDate(L, "short"), e.extra.duration_sec | duration]) | join(" · ") -%}
          {#- Rows of the other show say which show (like the badge on /listen/), and so does the player title. -#}
          {%- set otherShow = eShow and epShow and eShow.key != epShow.key -%}
          {%- set eFull = (eShow.short ~ " · " ~ et) if otherShow else et -%}
          <li class="flex grow items-center gap-3 py-3{{ ' max-sm:hidden' if loop.index > 2 }}">
            <span class="relative size-14 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-grape-soft text-grape">
              <span class="absolute inset-0 grid place-items-center" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "headphones", "size-5" %}</span>
              {#- the ≤480px copy the sync makes (extra.thumb) for a 56px tile, not the 1500–3000px cover art — and in
                  the tile its 256 px list copy when the sync made one (cmListThumb: "<name>.sm.webp", else the 480 px
                  file, unchanged). Not when the row's picture is the featured episode's: the episode card already loads
                  that 480 px file (80–160 px there), so the tile reuses it instead of a second download.
                  data-img below keeps the 480 px file (the player shows it in the episode card's square) and gets the
                  site's base from `url` (the base plugin rewrites src/href, never data-*) -#}
              {%- set eArt = e.extra.thumb or e.image -%}
              {%- set eTile = eArt if eArt == (ep.extra.thumb or ep.image) else (eArt | cmListThumb) -%}
              {% if eArt %}{{ img(eTile, "absolute inset-0 size-full object-cover") }}{% endif %}
            </span>
            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
              {#- (a weekly open meeting's short name is ours — in the page language, the Grapevine Weekly Open's always
                  English: shortLang; another show's is its own name, in its own language) -#}
              {% if otherShow %}<p class="truncate text-[0.68rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-grape"{% if eShow.shortLang != L %} lang="{{ eShow.shortLang }}"{% endif %}>{{ eShow.short }}</p>{% endif %}
              <p class="line-clamp-2 text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{{ et }}</p>
              <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-faint">{{ em }}{% if epMixed %} {{ ui.langPill(e, L) }}{% endif %}{% if e.extra.audio_bytes %}<span class="pwa-saver-only"> · <span class="sr-only">{{ "pwa.audio_size" | t(L) }} </span>{{ e.extra.audio_bytes | fileSize }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="font-semibold text-vine" x-show="isDone('{{ e.id }}')" x-cloak data-gv-say=" · {{ 'media.played' | t(L) }}" x-text="isDone('{{ e.id }}') ? $el.dataset.gvSay : ''"></span></p>
            </div>
            {% if e.extra.audio_url %}
            <a href="{{ e.extra.audio_url }}" class="home-play grid size-11 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-grape-soft text-grape transition"
               :class="isPlaying($el.dataset.id) && 'is-playing'"
               @click.prevent="play($el)" data-id="{{ e.id }}" data-src="{{ e.extra.audio_url }}" data-title="{{ eFull }}" data-meta="{{ [e.date | fmtDate(L, 'medium'), e.extra.duration_sec | duration] | join(' · ') }}" data-img="{{ (eArt | url) if eArt else '' }}"
               data-du="{{ e.extra.duration_sec or '' }}" data-sh="{{ e.extra.show or e.category or 'gv' }}" data-u="{{ e | mediaEpisodePage }}"
               aria-label="{{ 'home.play_episode' | t(L, { title: eFull }) }}">
              <span x-show="!isPlaying($el.parentElement.dataset.id)">{% icon "play", "size-5 translate-x-px" %}</span>
              <span x-show="isPlaying($el.parentElement.dataset.id)" x-cloak>{% icon "pause", "size-5" %}</span>
            </a>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {{ woLink | safe }}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if v %}
    {%- set vt = v | mediaTitle(L) -%}
    {%- set vse = v | mediaSE(L) -%}
    {%- set vWeekly = (v | mediaVideoKind) == "weekly" -%}
    {%- set vLv = v.category == "lv" or v.lang == "es" -%}
    {#- the strip (home.css .home-video): the video on the left — 40% of a phone's width, 13rem from 640px, 15rem from
        1024px —, its words beside it, "Subscribe on YouTube" on the right from 1024px (under the words from 640px) -#}
    <article class="home-video card{{ ' mt-6' if ep }}" aria-labelledby="video-title">
      <lite-youtube videoid="{{ v.extra.video_id }}" class="home-yt" playlabel="{{ 'home.video_play' | t(L, { title: vt }) }}" style="background-image: url('{{ v.extra.video_id | ytThumb }}');">
        <a href="{{ v.url }}" class="lyt-playbtn" title="{{ 'home.video_play' | t(L, { title: vt }) }}"><span class="lyt-visually-hidden">{{ "home.video_play" | t(L, { title: vt }) }}</span></a>
      </lite-youtube>
      <div class="home-video-info">
        <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="badge-grape">{% icon "youtube", "size-3" %} {{ "home.new_videos" | t(L) }}</span>
          {%- set vLabelLang = v | mediaMeetingLang(L) %}
          {% if vWeekly %}<span class="{{ 'badge-lv' if vLv else 'badge-grape' }}"{% if vLabelLang %} lang="{{ vLabelLang }}"{% endif %}>{% icon "users", "size-3" %} {{ v | mediaMeetingLabel(L) }}</span>
          {% elif vLv %}<span class="badge-lv">La Viña</span>{% endif %}
          {{ ui.langPill(v, L) }}
        </p>
        <h3 id="video-title" class="home-video-title font-display font-semibold leading-snug text-ink"{% if v.lang and v.lang != L and v.lang != "und" and vt == (v | mediaTitle(v.lang)) %} lang="{{ v.lang }}"{% endif %}>
          <a href="{{ v.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="line-clamp-2 no-underline hover:text-gv">{{ vt }}<span class="sr-only"> {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a>
        </h3>
        <p class="meta-row text-xs text-faint">
          {% if vse %}<span class="font-semibold text-gv">{{ vse }}</span>{% endif %}
          {% if v.date %}<time datetime="{{ v.date | isoDate }}">{{ v.date | fmtDate(L, ("month" if v.extra.date_approx else "short")) }}</time>{% endif %}
          {% if v.extra.duration_sec %}<span>{{ v.extra.duration_sec | duration }}</span>{% endif %}
          {% if v | machineFor(L) %}<span>{{ ui.autoNote(v, L) }}</span>{% endif %}
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="home-video-act"><a href="{{ site.links.youtube_channel }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-ghost btn-sm">{% icon "youtube", "size-4" %} {{ "home.youtube_subscribe" | t(L) }}<span class="sr-only"> {{ "home.opens_new_tab" | t(L) }}</span></a></p>
    </article>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{#- =====================================================================
    6. UPCOMING EVENTS — the next three, as date tiles (our two monthly meetings are in the cards at the top: the
       next committee meeting is left out here, and so is our Grapevine Meeting — homeEvents' 4th argument, the
       hero's series —, so their places go to other events). The Grapevine meetings of local groups have ONE home,
       /meetings/ — a header action here. Fewer than three: a "calendar on your phone" card fills the row.
    ===================================================================== -#}
{% set evs = D.events.items | homeEvents(meeting.next, 3, gm.key if gm else "") %}
{%- set gvmHome = db.meetings | cmGvMeetings(L, site) -%}
{% if evs.length %}
<section class="section pt-0" aria-labelledby="events-title" data-gv-expire-list>
  <div class="container-page">
    {% call ui.sectionHead("home.events_title" | t(L), "home.events_sub" | t(L), "/events/" | lurl(L), "home.events_all" | t(L), "calendar-days", { eyebrow: "home.events_eyebrow" | t(L), tone: "text-vine", id: "events-title", lang: L }) %}
    {% if gvmHome.inArea %}<a href="{{ '/meetings/#grapevine-meetings' | lurl(L) }}" class="btn-ghost btn-sm">{% icon "map-pin", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.gvm.home_title" | t(L) }}</a>{% endif %}
    {% endcall %}
    {#- grid-cols-1 on phones: a long place name (one truncated line) must not widen the column. -#}
    {%- set withCta = evs.length < 3 -%}
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" role="list">
      {% for e in evs %}
      {%- set x = e.extra or {} -%}
      {#- date tile, "when" line and place — the same rules as /events/ (a date RANGE for an event over
          several days, the place in the page language, "Venue to be announced" without a map pin) -#}
      {%- set info = e | homeEventInfo(L) -%}
      {#- the kind's colour, the same as on /events/ (eventTone: committee · gv · lv · booth · assembly · other) -#}
      {%- set tone = e | eventTone -%}
      {#- Its own page (since round 37: evHref, eleventy/filters/event-links.js — "/events/<anchor>/"); a monthly
          recurring event its series' page ("/events/series/<key>/"); a committee meeting its section on /meetings/.
          Already in the page's language (never through lurl again). -#}
      {%- set href = e | evHref(L, D, site) -%}
      {#- its title as /events/ shows it (cmTidyTitle); etRaw, the title before that, says whether it is the original's -#}
      {%- set etRaw = e | tx("title", L) -%}
      {%- set et = etRaw | cmTidyTitle -%}
      {#- the card hides itself once the event is over (GV.expire); the calendar card below is not an event -#}
      {%- set evEndAt = e | homeEventEnd -%}
      <li data-gv-expire-item{% if evEndAt %} data-gv-expire="{{ evEndAt }}"{% endif %}>
        <article class="card card-link ev-accent ev-tone-{{ tone }} group relative flex h-full gap-4 p-4 sm:flex-col sm:p-5">
          <div class="home-datetile{{ ' is-range' if info.tile.range }}" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="home-datetile-month">{{ info.tile.mon }}</span>
            <span class="home-datetile-day">{{ info.tile.day }}</span>
            <span class="home-datetile-wd">{{ info.tile.wd }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
              {#- names the kind in words — the same labels and icons as the /events/ badges, so colour is never the only signal -#}
              {%- set kindIcon = { committee: "users", gv: "grapes", lv: "grapes", booth: "store", assembly: "landmark", other: "map-pin" } -%}
              {%- if tone == "gv" and e.category == "gv-calendar" %}{% set kindLabel = "committee.events.badge_gv" | t(L) %}
              {%- elif tone == "lv" and e.category == "lv-calendar" %}{% set kindLabel = "committee.events.badge_lv" | t(L) %}
              {#- (a series of ours, e.g. the Grapevine Meeting: "NETA 65", never the name of a magazine that holds it —
                  event-tone.js; an online one with the camera, not the map pin) -#}
              {%- elif tone == "other" %}{% set kindLabel = ("committee.events.kind.neta" if e.category in ["neta65", "recurring"] else "committee.events.kind.event") | t(L) %}
              {#- (the Area's own events share one colour: an assembly says "Area assembly", as on /events/ — an ACM, a
                  town hall or a GSR/DCM orientation "Area event": event-tone.js isAssembly) -#}
              {%- elif tone == "assembly" %}{% set kindLabel = ("committee.events.badge_assembly" if (e | isAssembly) else "committee.events.kind.assembly") | t(L) %}
              {%- else %}{% set kindLabel = ("committee.events.kind." ~ tone) | t(L) %}{% endif %}
              {%- set kindIco = "video" if (tone == "other" and x.online_url and not x.city and not x.location) else kindIcon[tone] -%}
              <span class="badge ev-badge">{% icon kindIco, "size-3" %} {{ kindLabel }}</span>
              {% if info.tentative %}{{ ui.tentativeBadge(L) }}{% endif %}
              {% if e.lang and e.lang != L and e.lang != "und" and ((e | machineFor(L)) or etRaw == e.title) %}<span class="badge-muted uppercase" title="{{ ('lang.' ~ e.lang) | t(L) }}">{{ e.lang }}</span>{% endif %}
            </p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink"{% if e.lang and e.lang != L and e.lang != "und" and etRaw == e.title %} lang="{{ e.lang }}"{% endif %}>
              <a href="{{ href }}" class="no-underline after:absolute after:inset-0 group-hover:text-gv"{% if href.startsWith('http') %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ et }}</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="sr-only">{{ info.srDate }}</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
              {#- An outside calendar that only gives a date: the time isn't listed (same wording as /events/), not "all day". -#}
              <li class="flex items-start gap-1.5">{% set whenIcon = "calendar-range" if info.multiDay else "clock" %}{% icon whenIcon, "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}{{ info.when }}</li>
              {% if info.location and info.tba %}<li class="flex items-start gap-1.5 italic">{% icon "hourglass", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}<span class="min-w-0 line-clamp-2">{{ info.location }}</span></li>
              {% elif info.location %}{% set locIcon = "video" if (x.online_url and not x.city) else "map-pin" %}<li class="flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon locIcon, "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}<span class="min-w-0 line-clamp-2">{{ info.location }}</span></li>
              {#- online only (no place): "Online on Zoom", as on /events/ -#}
              {% elif info.online %}<li class="flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}<span class="min-w-0">{{ info.online }}</span></li>{% endif %}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
      {% if withCta %}
      <li>
        <article class="home-cal-cta card card-link group relative flex h-full flex-col gap-3 p-4 sm:p-5">
          <span class="grid size-11 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-vine-soft text-vine">{% icon "calendar-heart", "size-5" %}</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">
            <a href="{{ '/events/#subscribe' | lurl(L) }}" class="no-underline after:absolute after:inset-0 group-hover:text-vine">{{ "home.cal_cta_title" | t(L) }}</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "home.cal_cta_text" | t(L) }}</p>
          <p class="mt-auto inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 pt-1 text-sm font-semibold text-vine">{{ "home.cal_cta_link" | t(L) }} {% icon "arrow-right", "size-4 transition group-hover:translate-x-0.5" %}</p>
        </article>
      </li>
      {% endif %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{#- =====================================================================
    7. MORE ON THIS SITE — the pages that had sections of their own here until November 2026, one link each (the
       menus have them too): the committee's Bulletin, the Library, Published writers (the writers from our Area
       and Texas the magazines published), Instagram, the Portfolio, Photos — and Stay updated (the e-mail digest,
       the calendars, RSS, the app). Two columns on a phone (the names only: each page's line from 640px), four from 1024px.
    ===================================================================== -#}
{%- set moreLinks = [
  { url: "/bulletin/", icon: "megaphone", key: "nav.bulletin", desc: "nav.bulletin_desc" },
  { url: "/library/", icon: "library", key: "nav.library", desc: "search.page_desc.library" },
  { url: "/published/", icon: "award", key: "nav.published", desc: "nav.published_desc" },
  { url: "/instagram/", icon: "instagram", key: "nav.instagram", desc: "home.ig_sub" },
  { url: "/portfolio/", icon: "folder-open", key: "nav.portfolio", desc: "nav.portfolio_desc" },
  { url: "/photos/", icon: "images", key: "nav.photos", desc: "nav.photos_desc" },
  { url: "/stay-updated/", icon: "bell-ring", key: "nav.stay_updated", desc: "stay.short_desc" }
] -%}
<section class="section pt-0" aria-labelledby="more-title">
  <div class="container-page">
    <h2 id="more-title" class="h-section">{{ "home.more_title" | t(L) }}</h2>
    <ul class="home-more mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 lg:grid-cols-4" role="list">
      {% for m in moreLinks %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ m.url | lurl(L) }}" class="home-more-link card card-link group flex h-full items-center gap-3 p-3 no-underline sm:items-start sm:p-4">
          <span class="home-more-icon grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-gv-soft text-gv" aria-hidden="true">{% icon m.icon, "size-5" %}</span>
          <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <span class="block font-semibold leading-snug text-ink group-hover:text-gv">{{ m.key | t(L) }}</span>
            <span class="mt-0.5 block text-sm leading-snug text-muted max-sm:hidden">{{ m.desc | t(L) }}</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
